BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wé Ani - Burn That Bridge Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260909T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260909T230000
UID:874baab1deeb5ccb93ceceadd265d29c@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:Don’t be fooled by her tiny speaking voice\, because she tur
 ns into a power-house vocalist as soon as she touches the mic. Wé Ani (Wa
 y Ah-nee) is a remarkable singer and performer who captivated audiences ar
 ound the world with her extraordinary voice. Born with a gift for music\, 
 Wé Ani discovered her passion for singing at the tender age of 12. From t
 hat moment on\, her journey in the music industry began to unfold\, leadin
 g her to remarkable achievements and unforgettable experiences. Wé Ani's 
 talent caught the attention of many when she showcased her vocal prowess o
 n the hit TV show\, The Voice. Competing against an array of talented arti
 sts\, Wé Ani left an indelible mark and secured a remarkable 3rd place fi
 nish\, winning the hearts of viewers with her soulful and powerful perform
 ances. Prior to her appearance on The Voice\, Wé Ani honed her skills at 
 the prestigious Harlem School of the Arts\, refining her technique and dev
 eloping her unique style. Her dedication and hard work paid off when\, at 
 the age of 16\, she triumphed on four separate occasions at the renowned A
 pollo Theater in New York City\, solidifying her status as an exceptional 
 vocalist. Wé Ani's talent knows no bounds\, and her music has taken her a
 cross the United States and beyond. Sharing the stage with legendary artis
 ts such as Stevie Wonder\, Josh Groban\, Chris Botti\, Ceelo Green\, Patti
  Austin\, Dionne Warwick\, John Legend\, and Alicia Keys\, Wé Ani has pro
 ven herself to be a versatile and dynamic performer\, captivating audience
 s with her incredible vocal range and stage presence. Her talents have bee
 n recognized and celebrated on numerous prestigious platforms. Wé Ani had
  the honor of performing at the Gershwin Prize Tribute\, a tribute to the 
 legendary Tony Bennett\, held at the Library of Congress. She also showcas
 ed her skills in the rock and roll off-Broadway play Rocktopia\, where she
  shared the stage with renowned musician Dee Snider.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/oe7gng-w-ani-burn-that-bridge-tour-9th-sep-songb
 yrd-washington-dc-tickets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Guerilla Toss
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261020T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261020T230000
UID:4d73744fc644dd2352f3f882825ae662@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:When NYC-based experimental dance punks Guerilla Toss\, active
  since time immemorial aka 2011\, were in Vermont recording their new full
 -length album You’re Weird Now\, frontwoman Kassie Carlson would prepare
  what she called ‘punk lunch’: a communal meal made by raiding the stu
 dio fridge for whatever was left and assembling a sandwich from the most r
 andom ingredients imaginable. Regularly joining punk lunch were two legend
 s from their own corners of the weird music world: Stephen Malkmus (Paveme
 nt\, The Jicks) and Trey Anastasio\, Phish guitarist and owner of The Barn
 \; the recording studio where Guerilla Toss were making You’re Weird Now
 \, with Malkmus in the producer’s seat. Engineer Bryce Goggin\, who has 
 worked with Malkmus since Crooked Rain\, Crooked Rain\, and Ben Collette\,
  Phish’s longtime engineer at The Barn\, were also part of the crew. Whi
 le the idea of the guy from Phish and the guy from Pavement sitting around
  with Guerilla Toss\, congenially assembling sandwiches from random foodst
 uffs dug up from the depths of a studio fridge\, might seem absurd\, it al
 so makes total sense. Because really\, if there’s any band that serves a
 s the natural bridge between slacker punks who saw Pavement way before you
  did\, wild-eyed wooks who’ve seen Phish more times than you ever will\,
  and even the eccentrics in ’90s drip following former GT tourmates Prim
 us—it’s Guerilla Toss. A band so imaginative and unapologetically them
 selves\, they’re basically the real-life manifestation of a utopian\, po
 st-snob world where all musical ideas are worthy of expression and everyon
 e is welcome.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/avx2k7-guerilla-toss-20th-oct-songbyrd-washingto
 n-dc-tickets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:VOID & PHANTOM - Empire of Blood 2 Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260904T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260904T230000
UID:a1422e62bb661b1b506ff5bfc3e794a5@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:Friday September 4th VOID & PHANTOM - Empire of Blood 2 Tour w
 / Aphellion \\*\\*\\* Formed in 2019 by vocalist Jackson Davenport\, VOID 
 is a haunted\, technically sharp thrash/heavy metal force rising out of La
 fayette\, Louisiana. Blending razor-edged aggression with an eerie atmosph
 ere\, VOID stands at the crossroads of classic thrash intensity and dark\,
  theatrical heavy metal. The band made its first major statement with thei
 r debut album Horrors of Reality in early 2023. The record introduced VOID
 ’s uncompromising sound—fast\, intricate riffing\, commanding vocals\,
  and a sinister edge—and was followed by a relentless stretch of touring
  that hardened the band on the road and built a growing underground follow
 ing. That momentum led to VOID racking their first record deal\, and the b
 and then focused their efforts on crafting their most ambitious work to da
 te: Forbidden Morals\, a full-length concept album centered on a lost trav
 eler’s descent into the castle of Vlad the Impaler. Dark\, cinematic\, a
 nd technically ferocious\, the album marked a turning point for the band
 —putting VOID firmly on the map and opening the door to larger tours and
  wider recognition. Following the release of Forbidden Morals\, VOID signe
 d with Metal Blade Records to further carve their path in stone as one of 
 the most compelling new voices in modern traditional metal. For fans of: S
 avatage\, Metal Church\, King Diamond\, Annihilator\, Testament\, Lääz R
 ockit. \\*\\*\\* Aphellion are a four piece speed/thrash metal band hailin
 g from the suburbs of Maryland. Formed in 2023\, they have been cutting th
 eir teeth playing local shows since 2024 delivering their piercing and unr
 elenting speed/thrash sound to the masses. Along with blasting and talking
  metal records of the past in their dungeon\, they choose to pay their res
 pects by trying to keep the flame of old school metal alive. With leather 
 and spikes as armor they fight the good fight for old school heavy metal.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/2w5g37-void-phantom-empire-of-blood-2-tour-4th-s
 ep-songbyrd-washington-dc-tickets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Staring in Spaces (Single Release Show)
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261010T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261010T220000
UID:81d007fdeb7058a063e668322f1e33e5@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:Saturday October 10th Staring in Spaces (Single Release Show) 
 w/ Endlings \\+ FREE after party w/ DJ FIBI and Yoshmo! \\*\\*\\* Staring 
 in Spaces: The pop duo bringing infectious energy to the Nation's Capital.
  Childhood friends Jack Wright and William Lorenz began their musical jour
 ney in small-town Wisconsin\, quickly gaining momentum with their debut al
 bum Stop Talking. Now settled in D.C.\, Staring in Spaces released their b
 oldest and most ambitious album yet\, Kissing!\, at the end of 2024. Featu
 ring standout singles like the punchy "my mom/your dad" and the nostalgic 
 "Postcard\," the album pushes their pop sensibilities into rougher texture
 s and edgier performances. With a successful tour behind them and energize
 d audiences craving more. Wright and Lorenz are diving headfirst into 2026
 . \\*\\*\\* Endlings are four friends making music at the event horizon. D
 rawing on a wide and varied set of influences\, their music has emerged as
  raw and expansive\, dark and exploratory. They are making heads bang and 
 hearts throb at music venues across the D.C. metro area with a bleeding ed
 ge sound. The old world is dying\, and the new world struggles to be born:
  now is the time of monsters.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/avxoev-staring-in-spaces-single-release-show-10t
 h-oct-songbyrd-washington-dc-tickets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:tobi lou - Same Old Jeans Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260920T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260920T230000
UID:02a8bdebd2913cf7eabe64821148c9d8@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:tobi lou is a genre-blurring artist whose unique sound and ima
 ginative visuals have cemented him as a standout voice in today’s music 
 scene. Born in Nigeria and raised in Chicago\, tobi fuses hip-hop\, R&B\, 
 and pop with infectious melodies\, blending introspection with playful ene
 rgy that continues to captivate a loyal and growing fanbase. Before music\
 , tobi chased a career in professional baseball\, but an injury shifted hi
 s path—ultimately leading him to discover his true passion. His breakout
  single “Troop” introduced the world to his sound\, but it was the vir
 al success of “Buff Baby”—an ode to Adventure Time—that launched h
 im into the spotlight. The track became a massive hit on TikTok and is now
  RIAA certified Gold. tobi’s momentum carried into his first headline ru
 n—the sold-out 24-city Live on Ice Tour—which brought his signature st
 age presence to fans across the country. Later\, he delivered a standout h
 ometown performance at Lollapalooza that was widely praised by outlets lik
 e Hulu\, who named it one of the festival’s best sets. Beyond the music\
 , tobi is deeply involved in the creative direction of his work. He co-dir
 ects many of his visuals with longtime collaborator Glassface\, crafting a
  distinct aesthetic that’s become integral to his artistry. He also lead
 s his own fashion brand\, Farada\, which recently debuted its first origin
 al show—blurring the lines between music\, style\, and storytelling. His
  latest album\, Decent\, received widespread acclaim and features standout
  collaborations with fellow Chicago heavyweights Chief Keef\, Polo G\, and
  Saba\, as well as NBA All-Star Damian Lillard (aka Dame D.O.L.L.A). He al
 so teamed up with Young Thug on “Cobra\,” a smooth\, atmospheric track
  that reveals a more introspective side of tobi’s sound. Fresh off the s
 old-out Escape From Wiscansin Tour alongside R&B legend T-Pain\, tobi went
  on to headline his own 25-city run\, The Perish Blue Tour\, further cemen
 ting his reputation as a must-see performer. With unmatched versatility an
 d vision\, tobi lou isn’t just making music—he’s building a universe
  of his own.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/mxgo89-tobi-lou-same-old-jeans-tour-20th-sep-son
 gbyrd-washington-dc-tickets
