DESCRIPTION:Saturday August 22nd You Fool! (Single Release Show) w/ Kinoko
 \, NAYAN \\*\\*\\* You Fool! began in basements in the suburbs of Washingt
 on\, DC. Their unique blend of powerful indie rock and dreamy\, ethereal p
 ost-rock is so silky smooth you could sleep on it if you wanted to. But\, 
 you know what they say about sleeping on good music: don't! Their sound ha
 s been compared to the likes of 90's alternative legends The Cranberries a
 nd modern indie darlings Alvvays and Japanese Breakfast. Their debut EP\, 
 “What is the Meaning of This?”\, arrives in August 2024. \\*\\*\\* Nay
 an Bhula is a DC rock lifer who turned 50 and decided to get louder. A vet
 eran of post-punk outfit GIST and orchestrated indie ensemble The NRIs\, B
 hula has spent decades carving space for South Asian artists in rock ’n
 ’ roll—DIY\, defiant\, and relentless. His current band\, NAYAN\, blen
 ds DC post-punk urgency with classic rock swagger and ’80s new-wave hook
 s\, delivering high-octane live shows that surprise anyone expecting dad r
 ock (yes\, they’re dads—no\, it doesn’t slow them down). Recorded wi
 th J. Robbins at Magpie Cage\, new tracks arrive in early 2026. \\*\\*\\* 
 Kinoko: Diy emo music and art - self-conscious\, self-irreverent. Lotus ea
 ter core.
