UID:356f7b2053d93a24a2b5cb34331f1820@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:Friday September 25 Spoonfed (Single Release Show) w/ The Mont
 aines\, Aidan Leclaire \\*\\*\\* Spoonfed is a Washington\, D.C.-based roc
 k band consisting of Will Sevy (vocals/guitar)\, Kevin Cox (bass)\, and Ki
 eran O'Dell (vocals/drums). Formed in 2021 in the basement of their house 
 in Charlottesville\, Virginia\, Spoonfed has grown from late-night jam ses
 sions into one of the DMV's emerging indie bands. Spoonfed draws inspirati
 on from the grunge rock of the 1990s\, the alt-rock of the early 2000s\, a
 nd the grooves of modern funk. Expect energy: dark and uplifting melodies\
 , dynamic rhythms\, moody lyrics\, guitar solos. Their debut EP drops Sept
 ember 16. \\*\\*\\* Described as delivering “sticky guitar riffs and rom
 antic songs that sound like they belong on a 2014 Tumblr playlist\,” the
  band’s live show is nothing short of exhilarating. From slow-burning tr
 acks like “Helicopter” to their upcoming pop-forward releases\, The Mo
 ntaines channel the emotional weight and sonic ambition of artists like Th
 e 1975\, LCD Soundsystem\, and more — while carving out a space entirely
  their own.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
