BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:EMM
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260819T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260819T230000
UID:fb353e732afca099522a79ebd64497e7@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:EMM has built a reputation for creating music that showcases a
  woman’s unapologetic power in a world that constantly tries to diminish
  it. She has become a beacon of hope for girls everywhere who are searchin
 g for their inner heroine. EMM’s story is not a shallow one and it’s n
 ot for the faint of heart. In many ways\, from the outside looking in\, it
 ’s been a dream - a classically trained musical prodigy from a tiny Mich
 igan town\, graduating early\, moving to New York City on her own as a tee
 nager to pursue music\, and making it all a reality. EMM is an accomplishe
 d musician - an award-winning classical pianist\, guitarist\, songwriter a
 nd producer. Not to mention\, her voice and 4 octave vocal range - one tha
 t rivals the chart-topping divas of this generation. But as a young teen\,
  with all that creativity there was also an intense battle with shame\, gu
 ilt\, a chronic struggle with depression\, a challenging social life\, dee
 p familial struggles\, body image issues and religious and sexual trauma. 
 So songwriting was more than a passion or a discipline in EMM’s life - i
 t was the key to her survival. She crafted her first mixtape in 2016\, Bur
 ning In The Dark\, about her struggle with depression and suicidal ideatio
 n. She wrote\, sang\, produced\, performed\, played\, mixed\, and mastered
  the entire project top to bottom in her tiny North Hollywood apartment. S
 he then performed at some of the city’s largest arenas\, including the S
 taples Center and Dodger Stadium. She even secured features in USA Today\,
  Medium\, Earmilk\, and many more press outlets. Since 2018\, she has buil
 t an entire superhero story and universe that translates across 3 more mix
 tapes - “EMERALD\,” “RUBY\,” and “SAPPHIRE\,” with over 155 mi
 llion independent streams. “BLACK DIAMOND” is her next project in that
  series\, rolling out in 2024-2025. Her universe also includes an incredib
 le live show\, a doc\, a music video short film with over 5 million views\
 , and upcoming: a video game\, an animated series and a comic. And of cour
 se\, she’s built a catalog of hundreds of songs. She did all of this wit
 h no label\, completely self funded through her success as a content creat
 or. In 2024\, EMM released her documentary and full-length incredible conc
 ert project\, GENESIS\, which highlights the unique challenges of behind t
 he scenes women in entertainment. That project has been extremely viral wi
 th the clips reaching 100 million+ views online. In 2025\, EMM partnered w
 ith The Orchard and Independent (the label) for her next album\, BLACK DIA
 MOND. EMM called the album and visuals “a performance art piece designed
  to be a campy representation of the traits in women that are vilified mos
 t in society.” BLACK DIAMOND was met with critical acclaim from major ou
 tlets like GALORE\, ROLLING STONE\, and WONDERLAND. CAGERIOT said of her a
 ccompanying tour\, “EMM uses her platform to call out oppressive systems
 \, corporate\, religious\, and cultural\, that try to silence the vulnerab
 le. Her music isn’t just personal. It’s political. It's a protest wrap
 ped in an anthem... She delivers those themes through flawless choreograph
 y\, voice\, costume\, and presence\, all with the seamless precision of so
 meone trained for this moment their whole life with unwavering heart.” L
 ike a true alchemist\, EMM has turned the things that the industry and the
  world saw as an inconvenience- her vision\, her strong opinions\, her pow
 er\, and her honesty - into her superpowers. And this heroine is just gett
 ing started. When you ask EMM the question\, “What would you do if you w
 eren’t afraid?” Her answer appears to be\, “Just watch.” \\*\\*\\*
  Turning heartbreak into bangers and gay clubs into church\, Bentley Roble
 s has captivated fans worldwide with his infectious sound. With over 10 mi
 llion career streams and a fanbase that stans him like a main pop girl\, B
 entley has become one of the most exciting voices in indie pop. His acclai
 med EPs UGLY CRIER and CHAOTIC EROTICA earned major industry praise from S
 potify playlists like New Music Friday\, Fresh Finds\, and OBSESSED\, as w
 ell as press outlets like Wonderland\, NOTION\, and LADYGUNN. Hot off a so
 ld-out international tour with his TEARS & GEARZ bandmate ZEE MACHINE and 
 a 2025 Queerty nomination for Anthem of the Year\, Bentley is poised to be
  pop’s next breakout act. His highly anticipated debut album drops in 20
 26. \\*\\*\\* Calyope is the alter ego of Boston electronic artist Logan B
 uckley\, a genre-bending performer whose music unleashes the beasts of des
 ire\, pain\, and liberation. Combining sensuality\, chaos\, and soul\, Cal
 yope crafts electrifying shows that challenge how we see sexuality and hum
 anity. Think Charli XCX meets Lady Gaga with a shot of psychedelia—leavi
 ng audiences drenched in sweat\, freedom\, and a hunger for more.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/92gry6-emm-19th-aug-songbyrd-washington-dc-ticke
 ts
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LAERZ
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T230000
UID:974d19c1a70726182f8827ebd5ac11e5@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:LAERZ is an LA based electronic artist redefining what a DJ se
 t can be. Blurring the line between live production and performance\, he b
 uilds tracks in real time\, stacking cinematic vocals\, sculpting synths\,
  triggering drum pads\, and weaving loops into fully immersive\, high volt
 age moments. No two sets are the same. Every drop is built live. Every cho
 rus feels earned. He first captured global attention through his busking s
 tyle performances and on the spot content creation\, transforming sidewalk
 s and unexpected spaces into stages. That raw\, human approach resonated\,
  building a fiercely organic audience of over 4 million followers across s
 ocial media. That momentum translated offline as well\, culminating in a 2
 2 date headline tour that brought his immersive live show to audiences acr
 oss the country. What began as viral moments has evolved into something mo
 re focused: intentional releases crafted to live far beyond the scroll. So
 nically\, LAERZ exists where emotional depth meets dancefloor impact. His 
 current sound leans into break driven records that are percussive\, kineti
 c\, and built to move. Think the bounce and forward momentum of Daniel All
 an and Nimino layered with the wide\, ethereal vocal worlds of M83 and Emp
 ire of the Sun. The result is music that feels both massive and intimate\,
  pairing deep basslines and shimmering reverbs with stacked cinematic voca
 ls and rhythms that strike just as hard in a packed club as they do on a f
 estival stage at sunset. At his core\, LAERZ creates dance music that feel
 s human. Imperfect in the right ways. Emotional without losing its edge. I
 mmersive without sacrificing energy. Whether performing on a main stage\, 
 inside a dark club\, or curating a late night headphone session\, he deliv
 ers music meant to be felt\, not just heard. With a global audience behind
  him and a sharpened artistic vision ahead\, LAERZ is stepping into his mo
 st intentional era yet. The momentum is undeniable. The sound is evolving.
  And this is only the beginning.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/6dov9b-laerz-1st-oct-songbyrd-washington-dc-tick
 ets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The R&B Club Discusses The Legacy of Aaliyah
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260823T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260823T150000
UID:d0f019161e001279057cd4c016cbcf77@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:Certain moments in this century have stayed with us. And they 
 always will. August 25\, 2001\, is just that. It seems almost surreal to s
 ay\, but The R&B Club’s next event comes almost a quarter-century to the
  day that the R&B icon Aaliyah tragically passed away. There's no way not 
 to have a connection to her music\, but more importantly\, Aaliyah herself
 . If you know anything about us\, and what we pride ourselves on\, this wo
 n't be simply music being played. This is a voyage and a trip back in time
  into one of the most captivating and abbreviated careers in music history
 . We’ll discuss it all. The highs\, the classic records\, where we were 
 when we got the news of her death — and\, yes\, the R. Kelly of it all. 
 It's one time for Babygirl (better known as Aaliyah) on Sunday\, August 23
 \, at the only home we've ever known in Songbyrd. Tickets are $15 in advan
 ce and $20 at the door — pending there's any left. Come for the music. B
 ecause when’s the last time you heard “At Your Best (You Are Love)\,
 ” any of her classic records with Missy Elliott or Ginuwine\, or even 
 “I Care 4 U” in a room full of Aaliyah fans? Stay for the discussion. 
 Because we’re discussing it all. But leave with something even greater. 
 The world will always miss Aaliyah. But here at The R&B Club\, the story o
 f Aaliyah Dana Houghton will never\, ever be forgotten. \\*\\*\\* The R&B 
 Club is a cultural gathering founded in 2018 that discusses the influence 
 of R&B music. In other words\, think of it as a musical book club-style me
 etup. Follow us on social media at @therandbclubdc for more information.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/pywk9k-the-rb-club-discusses-the-legacy-of-aaliy
 ah-23rd-aug-songbyrd-washington-dc-tickets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
