SUMMARY:Kiefer
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T230000
UID:d7b8a4f6ab4ef645d8fe003f9b7bf8dd@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:Kiefer is an American pianist\, producer\, and composer whose 
 music bridges modern jazz\, hip-hop production\, and expressive solo piano
  traditions. His work has earned the rare distinction of being signed to b
 oth Stones Throw Records and Blue Note Records\, two of the most influenti
 al labels in hip-hop and jazz\, signaling his legitimacy and impact in bot
 h scenes. A Grammy Award–winning producer for his contributions to Malib
 u by Anderson .Paak\, he has collaborated with artists including Dr. Dre\,
  Kaytranada\, De La Soul\, Pete Rock\, Terrace Martin\, Kenny Beats\, Walt
 er Smith III\, and Nate Smith. Drawing from influences ranging from Herbie
  Hancock to Los Angeles beat-makers like Madlib\, Kiefer’s music balance
 s technical sophistication with emotional immediacy\, pairing lush harmony
  with minimalist\, hypnotic grooves. New music is on the way later this ye
 ar from him. \\*\\*\\* Shibo is the solo project of bassist and producer E
 rik Shiboski. A Bay Area native and a staple of the Northeast LA music com
 munity\, Shibo is a longtime friend and collaborator of Kiefer’s\, servi
 ng as a co-producer and primary artist on Kiefer’s upcoming album. His b
 ass playing and production are also featured in the work of BROCKHAMPTON\,
  Tkay Maidza\, Jay Prince\, Planet Giza\, Nick Dorian\, and others. His de
 but album\, featuring his unique brand of musicianship and synth psychedel
 ia\, is set to drop later this year.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/pynlkl-kiefer-3rd-oct-songbyrd-washington-dc-tic
 kets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
